        }
      ],
      "words": 32
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "To be positive every time she tried to kick the habit. To be the reason to stay alive",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2269
        }
      ],
      "words": 18
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "There weren’t ghosts around—that I saw, anyway—but there was a feeling that made me uncomfortable, like I was being watc",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2591
        }
      ],
      "words": 29
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "In other words, Franny did more for my mother in the last year of her life than I did",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3671
        }
      ],
      "words": 19
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "And then they went home, and I slept in Franny’s soft bed and cried into her silk pillowcases and wished Franny was my m",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4319
        }
      ],
      "words": 62
    },
    {
      "block": "原句12",
      "no": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I left Franny a note that my mother had died. It was the best I could do. Months later, Mark told me there was a message",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4640
        }
      ],
      "words": 35
    },
    {
      "block": "原句13",
      "no": 13,
      "segments": [
        {
